Since we're talking about coding styles and doing things the right way, let's talk about verification.

163
00:08:32,976 --> 00:08:37,534
这不完全是一个功能或命令，它更像是一种工作流和最佳实践。
This isn't exactly a feature or a command, it's more so a workflow and best practice.

164
00:08:37,808 --> 00:08:44,288
我给这个评 S tier，甚至要是双 S 或者三 S 也不为过，因为这不仅仅是 AI 的问题。
And I'm giving this an S tier, and if anything, a double S or even a triple S because this isn't just an AI thing.

165
00:08:44,368 --> 00:08:46,448
这纯粹就是良好的软件工程基础。
This is just good software engineering fundamentals.

166
00:08:46,608 --> 00:08:48,288
AI 只是让这一点变得更加重要。
AI just makes this more important.

167
00:08:48,462 --> 00:08:50,208
那么，验证到底是什么？
So, what exactly is verification?

168
00:08:50,368 --> 00:08:55,088
本质上，你是在给 Claude 提供一种方法，让它在认为任务完成之前先检查自己的工作。
Essentially, you're giving Cloud a way to check its own work before it considers something done.

169
00:08:55,168 --> 00:08:57,316
它其实根本不知道自己写得对不对。
It actually has no idea if it's correct.

170
00:08:57,488 --> 00:09:02,448
但有了验证，它就能写出代码并检查它是否真的正确，而不仅仅是告诉你它做完了。
But with verification, it can write the code and see if it's actually correct, not just telling you it's done.

171
00:09:02,608 --> 00:09:06,128
现在有多种验证方法，最明显的一种就是测试。
Now there's multiple ways to verify, and the most obvious one is tests.

172
00:09:06,208 --> 00:09:07,968
但一定要确保你正确地进行测试。
But make sure you do tests correctly.

173
00:09:08,174 --> 00:09:10,848
告诉 Claude 先写测试，然后再去实现。
Tell Claude to write the test first and then implement.

174
00:09:11,008 --> 00:09:11,648
这一点很重要。
This is important.

175
00:09:11,822 --> 00:09:16,688
如果你让它先实现再写测试，它只会写出能通过它自己代码的测试。
If you tell it to implement first and then write the test, it's just going to write tests that pass its own code.

176
00:09:16,814 --> 00:09:18,848
那不叫测试，那叫作弊。
And that's not exactly testing, that's cheating.

177
00:09:19,008 --> 00:09:22,768
确保不要测试每一行代码，只测试最重要的部分。
Make sure you don't test every single line, just test the most important things.

178
00:09:22,958 --> 00:09:29,328
我注意到像更聪明的模型，喜欢去测试每一件没必要的事情，这会把你的代码库搞得臃肿不堪。
I've noticed that smarter models like to test every single thing when
it's really not necessary and it kind of just bloats your code base.

179
00:09:29,488 --> 00:09:32,288
其他的验证方法还有类型检查器和代码检查工具。
Some other ways to verify are type checkers and linters.

180
00:09:32,448 --> 00:09:36,048
如果你的语言支持的话，告诉 Claude 在认为任务完成之前先运行它们。
If your language supports it, tell Claude to run it before considering the task done.

181
00:09:36,208 --> 00:09:44,288
另外两种验证方法，如果你在做前端和设计工作的话，就
是截图测试和浏览器测试，因为 Claude 实际上是瞎子。
Two other ways you can do verification, and this is if you're doing front-end and design work,
is screenshot testing and testing with the browser because Claude is literally blind.

182
00:09:44,368 --> 00:09:46,208
它根本看不见自己正在做出的东西。
It can't actually see what it's making.

183
00:09:46,368 --> 00:09:52,608
有了这两种验证方法，Claude 就能真的打开你的应
用，到处点点，截点图，并看到实际发生了什么。
With these two verification methods, Claude can actually open your app,
click around, get some screenshots, and actually see what's happening.

